extraction_notes: |
  - Printed 38-43. The Giants section opens on printed 38, its shared combat paragraph is at the top of printed 40, the Gigantes entry and its block, headed "Giant, Monstrous Humanoids (mutants even by giant standards)", are on printed 42 with the mutation table, and the insanity table is at the top of printed 43. Folios read off the renders.
  - Attributes as printed on 42: I.Q. 2D6, M.E. 1D6, M.A. 2D6, P.S. 4D6+8 (supernatural), P.P. 3D6+6, P.E. 4D6+6, P.B. 2D6, Spd 4D6. Hit Points "P.E. +1D6 per level of experience".
  - S.D.C. reads "1D6x10 plus possible mutation variations that provide bonus S.D.C. as well as those acquired from physical skills": the 1D6x10 is a pool bonus rolled once, and no sdc_base is stated. Each mutation''s S.D.C. is a pool bonus on its own row.
  - Horror Factor prints "13 and higher depending on their appearance": 13 is stored as horror_factor and the open upper end is a natural ability. The book gives no figure per mutation.
  - Average P.P.E. 2D4x10 as ppe_base; the line names no magic O.C.C. alternative. The block prints no Natural A.R.
  - Attacks per Melee reads "2 or by O.C.C. and corresponding combat skills": stored as attacks_base 2. Bonuses line: +4 to save vs Horror Factor, "plus other bonuses from attributes, O.C.C. skill bonuses and mutations". Stored.
  - SECTION RULE, printed 40 ("Special Combat Considerations and Bonuses"): the damage figures are the natural ability Giant Damage. The same paragraph says "most giants are also" +1 initiative, +2 pull punch, +1 roll with impact or fall, +3 save vs Horror Factor and +1 save vs poison, drugs and disease. It says "most", and every giant''s own Bonuses line restates part of that list with its own numbers, so the section list is NOT added to bonuses on any of the four giants; it is the natural ability Giant Bonuses (section rule), in the same words on each.
  - O.C.C.s Available: "Any men of arms, clergy, or witch". Stored as an `only` of the two groups and the witch. Magic prints "Generally unavailable". Printed 215: giants use the experience table of their chosen O.C.C., so no xp_table.
  - THE MUTATION TABLE is a `rolls: 4` group of twenty-one band-named options. Printed 42 heads it "Roll four times to determine random abilities and features" and prints 21 rows: 01-05, 06-10, 11-15, 16-20, 21-22, 23-24, 25-26, 27-32, 33-40, 41-45, 46-50, 51-54, 55-59, 60-64, 65-69, 70-75, 76-80, 81-84, 85-90, 91-95, 96-00 - 01-00 with no gap or overlap, each band and figure read off the render. Stored as bonuses: +20 S.D.C. (16-20), +1 attack (27-32), +1D6x10 S.D.C. (33-40), +6D6 S.D.C. (41-45), +2 initiative (51-54), +15 S.D.C. (65-69), +1D4x10 Spd (96-00). The second mouth''s extra attack applies only while an opponent is in reach, so it is prose; so are the bite, horn, tail, claw, breath and acid damages, the two flight chances and speeds, and the extra leg''s +20% to balance. The page says nothing about a repeated result.
  - Row 01-05 prints "Nightvision of 90 to 540 (3D6x30) feet"; 3D6x30 does span 90 to 540.
  - THE INSANITY TABLE is a `choose: 1` group of six band-named options. Printed 43 prints 01-10 psychosis, 11-34 no insanity, 35-44 obsession, 45-77 phobia, 78-91 neurosis, 92-00 affective disorder - 01-00 with no gap or overlap. Each row names a kind of insanity and nothing more; which psychosis, phobia and so on is left to the core rules. The later rolls (trauma, every 50 years) are in the group''s note.
  - Languages: "All speak Giantese. Some also speak troll and/or Gobblely." Giantese is the catalog''s Language: Troll/Giant, stored at 98 as this import''s reading of a spoken native tongue; no percentage is printed. Gobblely is "some", so it is not granted.
  - Natural Abilities prints "40 feet (12 m)" with the word nightvision missing; read as nightvision. "Instinctive swimmers (60%)" is a Swimming grant at the printed 60.
  - No money or equipment line is printed for the race; none is stated.
  - Size 15 to 20 feet, 14 feet plus 1D6 additional feet, 1,000 to 2,000 pounds; life span 150 years, few beyond 200. In the Lore.
